-- title:
--   The crossing model W[[u,v]]/(uv-π) is Noetherian
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is Noetherian, and let $\pi$ be an element of $W$. Consider the ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ of formal power series in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$, and inside it the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W π` generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, where $\pi$ is viewed in the power series ring via the constant-coefficient inclusion. The quotient of the two-variable power series ring by this ideal is the type `UVCrossingModel W π`, that is, $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$. The assertion is that this quotient ring is Noetherian: every ideal of $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ is finitely generated, equivalently its ideals satisfy the ascending chain condition.
--
--   This is the elementary finiteness input for the local crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, which arises as the complete local ring at a supersingular point of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-moduli problem in the Deligne–Rapoport description, where the special fibre acquires an ordinary double point. Together with the computation of its Krull dimension it feeds the regularity and normality statements for this local model, and it is invoked widely in the treatment of the node annulus and of localisations of the crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_isNoetherianRing.lean

